<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ciudad Vieja</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ciudad Vieja is a town in the Almolonga valley of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a>, the site of the second Spanish capital, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a> de los Caballeros, founded there in 1527. On the night of 10–11 September 1541 a flood of water and mud from the Volcán de Agua destroyed the city, killing the governor Beatriz de la Cueva. The capital was then moved to the nearby Panchoy valley, today <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antigua-guatemala">Antigua Guatemala</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ciudad-vieja.jpg" alt="Ciudad Vieja" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rene Hernandez · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ciudad_Vieja_-_Skyline.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
